<html><title>Destinies</title>
<h1>Destinies: The Paperback Magazine of Science Fiction and Speculative Fact</h1>

<pre>
From the back cover of Destinies, Nov/Dec 1978:

    "Welcome to the future - welcome to Destinies

    YOU are about to embark on a wholly new concept in the publication of
    science fiction: the very first issue of the very first PAPERBACK 
    science fiction magazine.

    In this and succeeding issues of DESTINIES you will find the best in 
    CURRENT science fiction - stories of profound insight and High
    Adventure by such renowned authors as ... and virtually all the 
    other contemporary writers who have made - and are making - science
    fiction what it is ... and what it will become. These are the writers
    who give shape and substance to our dreams - and it is from our
    dreams that the future itself takes form.

    But it is not just great fiction that will make up the pages of
    DESTINIES; this is the magazine of science fiction and SPECULATIVE 
    FACT. In it you will find something even scarcer than solid
    exciting science fiction: <i>non-fiction for the science fiction reader</i> 
    - Speculative Fact, if you will."
</pre>
<p>
Destinies was published in standard paperback format for 11 issues between
1978 and 1981.  There was a subsequent series of anthologies, also 
edited by James Baen, entitled "New Destinies".
